 "notes": [
  "Schema 3. Renames since schema 1, key by key: row key seeds -> n (matching the drift artifact); ground label 50 -> rough_50mm; protocol.command from [vx, vy, wz_text] to an object; protocol.controller removed and published per row as controller; cross_abs_median -> open_cross_median_abs / closed_cross_median_abs; cross_abs_max -> open_cross_max_abs / closed_cross_max_abs; heading_median_deg -> open_heading_median_abs_deg / closed_heading_median_abs_deg; control_steps_median -> open_control_steps_to_10m_median / closed_control_steps_to_10m_median. The pure_pursuit rows take the same renames and additionally gained open_* reference columns, so schema 1's cross_abs_median / cross_abs_max / per_seed_cross_m there became closed_cross_median_abs / closed_cross_max_abs / per_seed_closed_cross_m.",
  "cross values are metres, signed along the start heading's left axis, at the 10 m step. heading values are the heading change wrapped to +-180 degrees. per_seed_*_cross_m keeps the sign of each seed.",
  "Two aggregation families live here. The cross and heading keys publish medians of absolute values and say so with an _abs segment; open_control_steps_to_10m_median, closed_control_steps_to_10m_median and closed_saturated_fraction_median are ordinary medians over the same n seeds and carry no _abs. Every *_max_abs is the single worst seed. The drift artifact publishes signed cross and heading medians instead, so the two files differ for a cell whose seeds straddle the line: base on rough_50mm is cross_median -2.27 m and heading_median_deg 29.46 there, against cross_median_abs 4.27 m and heading_median_abs_deg 46.02 here. The signed median cancels opposing drift; the absolute one measures how far off the line each run ended up.",
  "Every row in rows[] and pure_pursuit[] carries controller (heading hold / pure pursuit) as a per-row constant. lookahead_m is the single key that appears only on the pure_pursuit rows, because a heading hold has none.",
  "The loop reads the simulator's heading_w. A deploy-side loop reads an IMU or an estimate, so these numbers are upper bounds.",
  "base under pure pursuit is the one row where the worst seed improves strongly (1.07 -> 0.50 m) while the median barely moves (0.18 -> 0.14 m)."
 ]
